<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Atlas Lab</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f4f7fb;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --surface-alt: #eaf0f7;
      --text: #14263b;
      --muted: #5f7389;
      --line: #d8e1ec;
      --accent: #1e6bd6;
      --accent-soft: #dbe8fb;
      --shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(16, 41, 70, 0.08);
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      color: var(--text);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(30,107,214,0.08), transparent 24rem),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #eff4fa 0%, var(--bg) 100%);
    }
    a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .shell { max-width: 1140px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    .topbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 10;
      backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
      background: rgba(244, 247, 251, 0.88);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(216, 225, 236, 0.85);
    }
    .topbar-inner {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 18px 0;
    }
    .brand {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }
    .brand span { color: var(--accent); }
    .nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 18px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .nav a:hover,
    .nav a:focus-visible { color: var(--accent); }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(280px, 0.9fr);
      gap: 28px;
      padding: 72px 0 28px;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 18px 0 18px;
      font-size: clamp(42px, 7vw, 78px);
      line-height: 0.96;
    }
    .lead {
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0 0 28px;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .actions {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 14px;
    }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      min-height: 46px;
      padding: 0 18px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--surface);
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .button.primary {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #fff;
      box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(30, 107, 214, 0.24);
    }
    .hero-panel,
    .card,
    .notice,
    .footer-box {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 24px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .hero-panel { padding: 22px; }
    .panel-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }
    .stat {
      padding: 14px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: var(--surface-alt);
    }
    .stat strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      font-size: 22px;
    }
    section { padding: 26px 0; }
    .section-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: end;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .section-head h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    }
    .section-head p {
      max-width: 520px;
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .grid-3 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 18px;
    }
    .card { padding: 22px; }
    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 22px;
    }
    .card p,
    .card li,
    .notice p,
    .footer-box p {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .list {
      margin: 14px 0 0;
      padding-left: 18px;
    }
    .notice {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 18px;
      padding: 24px;
    }
    .timeline {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }
    .timeline li {
      padding: 12px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .timeline li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .footer { padding: 32px 0 64px; }
    .footer-box {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 20px;
      padding: 22px 24px;
    }
    .footer-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .hero, .notice, .grid-3 {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
      .section-head, .footer-box, .topbar-inner {
        display: block;
      }
      .nav, .footer-links { margin-top: 14px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="shell topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">Atlas <span>Lab</span></a>
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#capabilities">Capabilities</a>
        <a href="#programs">Programs</a>
        <a href="#updates">Updates</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="top" class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Applied Communications Research</span>
        <h1>Quiet delivery systems for modern field teams.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Atlas Lab supports compact organizations that need dependable web presence,
          staged rollouts, and controlled access surfaces without publishing heavy
          operational detail.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="#capabilities">View capabilities</a>
          <a class="button" href="#updates">Latest program notes</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-panel" aria-label="Operational summary">
        <strong>Current focus</strong>
        <p>Regional edge readiness, archive-safe publishing flows, and low-noise support windows for distributed deployments.</p>
        <div class="panel-grid">
          <div class="stat"><strong>12</strong>Active research tracks</div>
          <div class="stat"><strong>5d</strong>Typical review cadence</div>
          <div class="stat"><strong>24/6</strong>Scheduled monitoring windows</div>
          <div class="stat"><strong>3</strong>Supported intake modes</div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="capabilities">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Core capabilities</h2>
        <p>Small, repeatable service patterns designed for low-friction delivery and predictable maintenance on modest infrastructure footprints.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Delivery surfaces</h3>
          <p>Static and semi-managed publishing fronts tuned for low maintenance, branded continuity, and regional edge compatibility.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Operational review</h3>
          <p>Configuration review for routing, exposure reduction, fallback behavior, and staged service activation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Maintenance windows</h3>
          <p>Planned changes grouped around certificate lifecycles, content refreshes, and service continuity checks.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="programs">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Program lanes</h2>
        <p>Each engagement is scoped around a practical support track rather than bespoke custom delivery from scratch.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="notice">
        <div>
          <h3>Standard engagement flow</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Initial intake and surface audit</li>
            <li>Controlled rollout plan with fallback points</li>
            <li>Verification window after deployment changes</li>
            <li>Short-form handoff notes for local operators</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Best suited for</h3>
          <p>Editorial groups, small labs, private research teams, and independent programs that need dependable public-facing continuity with minimal ceremony.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="updates">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Program updates</h2>
        <p>A lightweight bulletin board for release windows, intake pauses, and review-cycle notices.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <ul class="timeline">
          <li><strong>April cycle:</strong> documentation refresh and edge review windows are open for existing accounts.</li>
          <li><strong>March cycle:</strong> archive packaging flow moved to a single review handoff model.</li>
          <li><strong>February cycle:</strong> scheduled maintenance notices were consolidated into one support bulletin.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer id="contact" class="footer shell">
    <div class="footer-box">
      <div>
        <strong>Atlas Lab</strong>
        <p>Independent communications systems practice focused on quiet delivery and controlled operational change.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="#top">Top</a>
        <a href="#capabilities">Capabilities</a>
        <a href="#programs">Programs</a>
        <a href="#updates">Updates</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
